    "body": "<!-- claude-projects-attribution: {\"github_login\":\"siainbuletin\"} -->\n_Requested by **Sia** · [project thread](https://claude.ai/code/project/chan_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2?thread=cmsg_01KaQfLZaF43QUMN3kcT7pW2TDvuJ2KygqHcBPtkDgePBK)_\n\nStep 1 of 5 of the DEVONthink design. **Base: `main`.** Stack: #414 → #415 → #418 → #419 → #420 (merge in this order).\n\n## What\n- New module `sp-devonthink` (literate doc `docs/tangles/academic/sp-devonthink.org`, required from `sp-academic`, README row). It builds on `sp-reading` (citekey→UUID cache, item URLs, `osascript`).\n- `devonthink:UUID::PAGE` Org link: follow opens the record at the page (page counted from 1 in the link, `?page=N-1` in the URL); export writes the description (`key p. 6`).\n- `#+devonthink: UUID` litnote keyword: `sp-devonthink-set-keyword` writes it (asks before replacing a different value); `sp-devonthink-open-from-note` opens the record from the keyword, or by citekey when it is missing.\n- `sp-devonthink-insert-link`, `sp-devonthink-store-link` (record, page and selection shown in DEVONthink, for `org-insert-link`), and a `citar` Embark action `D`.\n- Keys under `C-c k d`: `o` open from note, `l` insert link, `s` store link, `k` set keyword, `r` refresh cache.\n\n## Not tested\n- The AppleScript of `sp-devonthink-store-link` (`current page` / `selected text` of the front `think window`) and the name of the citar Embark map were not run on the Mac.\n- Tested here: 14 ERT tests (Emacs 29.3) and the tangle check.\n\n## Manual testing\nRun on the Mac (fish, `~/.config/emacs-modular`), DEVONthink open on `literature`. Tick each box as you go.\n- [x] Check out: `cd ~/dotfiles; git fetch origin 414-devonthink-core; git checkout 414-devonthink-core`, restart Emacs.\n- [x] Unit tests: `cd ~/.config/emacs-modular; emacs -Q --batch -L libraries/modules/academic -l ert -l tests/sp-devonthink-test.el -f ert-run-tests-batch-and-exit` → `Ran 14 tests, 14 results as expected`.\n- [x] `M-x sp-reading-refresh` → message \"sp-reading: N PDFs in literature\".\n- [ ] In a scratch Org buffer, `C-u M-x sp-devonthink-insert-link`, choose e.g. `harrison-2010-therborn-post-marx`, page `6` → inserts `[[devonthink:<UUID>::6][harrison-2010-therborn-post-marx p. 6]]`.\n- [ ] `C-c C-o` on that link → DEVONthink comes to front on that record at page 6 (URL anchor `?page=5`). Note if off by one.\n- [ ] Export (`C-c C-e t u`) shows `harrison-… p. 6` without the UUID.\n- [x] In the litnote for that key: `C-c k d k` → `#+devonthink: <UUID>` appears below `#+title:`; run again → \"Keyword already set\". Save and check `git diff` in `~/notes` shows only that line.\n- [x] `C-c k d o` opens the record; `C-u C-c k d o` with page `3` opens page 3.\n- [x] Delete the keyword line, `C-c k d o` still opens (lookup by citekey).\n- [ ] In DEVONthink open a PDF page and select a sentence; in Emacs `C-c k d s` → \"Stored key p. N (selection in the kill ring)\"; `C-c C-l` offers the link; `C-y` pastes the quote. If the page is off by one, set `sp-devonthink-store-page-offset` to 1 or -1 and report. (Untested AppleScript.)\n- [ ] In a citar Embark menu on a key, press `D` → the record opens (`C-u` asks for a page). If `D` is missing, report `C-h v citar-embark-map`.\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n\nhttps://claude.ai/code/session_01WWLNiDWYwkgX4eqm2SVoTC\n",
